    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/fcd4933c-99bf-44b1-99fb-8ed7f53fb781-image.png\" style=\"width: 323px; height: 220px;\" /></p><p>Since, the vertex of the hyperbola are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>&#8242;</mi></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>Hence, the transverse axis of the hyperbola is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo></math> axis and centre is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>Equation of hyperbola can be taken as</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> and <math><mi>a</mi><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Since, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>Hence, equation of hyperbola is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Clearly, point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math> doesn&#39;t lies on the hyperbola.</p>",
